# Claims Module — Angular Frontend

## General Rules (ALL mandatory)
- Angular 18+ with lazy-loaded feature modules
- Angular Material + custom primary color palette (not default indigo)
- Reactive Forms ONLY — no template-driven forms
- ALL API calls via typed Angular service layer — NO direct HttpClient in components
- HTTP interceptor adds `Authorization: Bearer {token}` to ALL outgoing requests
- All API errors caught at service layer → displayed via `MatSnackBar` (success=green, error=red, warning=amber)
- All async operations show `mat-spinner` or skeleton loader; buttons disabled during pending calls
- Form validation via `mat-error` inside `mat-form-field`
- Responsive layout: usable at **1280px+** minimum width (FRS §11.4)

## Feature Modules (lazy-loaded)
- `ClaimsListModule` → `/claims`
- `ClaimDetailModule` → `/claims/:id`
- `FnolIntakeModule` → `/claims/new`

## Mock Auth Service (hardcoded — no real auth needed)
- 3 fixed users: `handler`, `supervisor`, `manager`
- Header shows **logged-in user name and role** (FRS §11.4) plus role switcher for testing
- JWT via `POST /api/auth/token`; HTTP interceptor reads token from AuthService

## Screen 1: Claims List Dashboard (`/claims`)
### Required Columns
- Claim Number | Policy Number | Client Name | Loss Date | Cause of Loss | Status badge | Total Reserve Amount

### Status Badge Colours (mandatory)
| Status | Colour |
|---|---|
| Draft | grey |
| Open | blue |
| UnderInvestigation | orange |
| PendingPayment | purple |
| Closed | green |
| Reopened | amber |
| Withdrawn | dark grey |

### Filter Bar
- Status: multi-select dropdown
- Date range: Loss Date from/to (date pickers)
- Assigned Handler: text search
- Cause of Loss: dropdown from `GET /api/reference/cause-of-loss-codes`

### Other
- Each row clickable → `/claims/:id`
- "Log New Claim" primary button → `/claims/new`
- Show total count + page size selector
- Empty state message when no results

## Screen 2: FNOL Intake Form (`/claims/new`)
Multi-step stepper. Each step validates INDEPENDENTLY before advancing.

### Step 1 — Policy & Loss Details
- Policy search: typeahead; calls `GET /api/policies/search?q=...`; dropdown of results
- On selection: populate PolicyNumber, ClientName, effective/expiration dates
- In-force indicator: green = within period, amber = outside or expired
- "Unknown Policy" toggle: proceeds with `PolicyId = null` (Warning shown)
- Loss Date: date-time picker + instant validation for BR-C-01 (not in future)
- Cause of Loss: searchable dropdown from reference API
- Loss Description: textarea with character counter (min 20 chars — BR-C-07)
- Loss Location: free text
- Estimated Loss Amount: optional numeric

### Step 2 — Parties & Risk Objects
- "Add Party" → inline form: Role (Claimant/Insured/ThirdParty/Witness/Attorney), Type (Person/Company), name, email, phone
- At least one Claimant required — inline warning if none
- Added parties shown as styled chips; remove button per chip
- "Add Risk Object" → inline form: Asset Type, Asset Description, Damage Description, Reference
- Risk objects shown as styled chips
- **Advisory** if no risk objects added (FRS §11.2): at least one recommended; does not block claim creation or Open transition (BR-C-08 Warning)

### Step 3 — Initial Reserve & Review
- Optional reserve: Component dropdown + Amount + real-time authority indicator:
  - ≤ $10,000 → "✓ Auto-approved"
  - > $10,000 ≤ $100,000 → "⚠ Supervisor approval required"
  - > $100,000 → "⚠ Manager approval required"
- Read-only review summary of all entered data
- "Create Claim" button disabled until Steps 1 and 2 valid
- Confirmation dialog if any Warning validation issues
- On success: navigate to `/claims/:id` + success banner/snackbar displaying generated **Claim Number** and link to detail (FRS §11.3)

## Screen 3: Claim Detail (`/claims/:id`)

### Header (always visible)
- Claim Number (prominent, copyable)
- Status chip (colour-coded)
- Policy Number + Client Name
- Loss Date + Cause of Loss
- Assigned Handler
- Status Transition button: dropdown of valid next statuses → confirmation dialog
  - For → Closed: pre-flight checklist showing CC-01–CC-04 status

### Tab 1 — Overview
Loss event fields (date, description, location, cause), severity badge, estimated amount, editable notes

### Tab 2 — Parties
Party list with role badge, contact info, active status. "Add Party" button. Remove button (disabled for last Claimant).

### Tab 3 — Reserves
- Summary cards: one per component (CurrentBalance + PendingAmount in amber if pending)
- Transaction table: Date | Type | Component | Amount (green/red) | Status badge | Submitted By | Approved By | GL Status
- GL Status badge: Pending | Posted | Failed (with retry)
- "Add Reserve" → slide-in form with Component, Amount, Reason + real-time authority indicator
- Per PendingApproval row:
  - **Approve button**: ONLY visible to `supervisor` or `manager` role
  - **Reject button**: ONLY visible to `supervisor` or `manager` role
  - **Retract button**: visible to the submitter of their own transaction
  - Handler role: NO Approve/Reject buttons shown

### Tab 4 — Documents
- List: name, type, date, uploader, size + download button (SAS URL → new tab)
- Upload button → file picker → multipart POST → progress indicator

### Tab 5 — Audit Log
- Reverse-chronological paginated list
- Per entry: timestamp | EventType badge | description | user | related entity
- Read-only; no editing

## Typed Angular Service Layer
```typescript
ClaimsService:     getAllClaims(filters), getClaimById(id), createClaim(command), transitionStatus(id, command)
ReserveService:    getReserves(claimId), openReserve(claimId, cmd), approveReserve(claimId, txnId), rejectReserve(claimId, txnId, reason), retractReserve(claimId, txnId)
PolicyService:     searchPolicies(query), getCoverageTypes(policyId)
ReferenceService:  getCauseOfLossCodes(perilCategory?), getClaimStatuses()
DocumentService:   uploadDocument(claimId, file), getDocuments(claimId)
AuditService:      getAuditLog(claimId, page)
AuthService:       getCurrentUser(), getToken(), switchRole(role) [mock only]
PartyService:      addParty(claimId, cmd), removeParty(claimId, partyId)
```
